      "id": "f1-default-shape",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-2-2",
      "summary": "The spec says a project without tests: reads \"with tests: {} and gateRuns: spec\"; the code returns tests: { gateRuns: \"spec\" } (config.mjs:15). Read literally, tests: {} and gateRuns inside tests (criterion spec-2-1) cannot both hold.",
      "assumption": "The phrase means \"no commands, gateRuns spec\". The implemented shape is the only one that agrees with spec-2-1 and with the coordinator consumer (testSettings returns readConfig(root).tests). Worth one word in spec 14 setup text if it quotes the default."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-flow-map-fixture",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "criterion": "spec-2-1",
      "summary": "The spec check writes the fixture as a flow map (tests: { ... }); the YAML subset has no flow maps and refuses that line by number, so the test writes the same values in block form (tests/runtime-config-tests.test.ts:26-27, with a comment saying why).",
      "assumption": "The check names the values, not the YAML style; block form tests the stated behavior. Adding flow maps to the parser is out of this spec's file list."
    },
